# Copy this file to .env and adjust for your machine. react-native-config
# reads .env at native build time (Android/iOS) — after changing it you must
# rebuild the app, a JS-only reload is not enough.
#
# - Android emulator: the emulator's virtual host maps to your machine's
#   localhost via 10.0.2.2, so point at that instead of "localhost".
# - iOS simulator: it shares your Mac's network stack, so "localhost" works
#   directly.
# - Physical device (either platform): "localhost"/10.0.2.2 both refer to
#   the device itself, not your dev machine — use your machine's LAN IP
#   (e.g. http://192.168.1.23:5000/api/v1) and make sure the device is on
#   the same network as the backend.
API_BASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2:5000/api/v1
